greeter: Don't quit when the last window closes

Backport of upstream SDDM commit da0b64d8e2378c4bce16cbea6cac2ffc89ad1a4a
by Daniel Betz <dnlbtz@gmail.com> (2026-08-12), which is on develop and not in
v0.21.0. 9Spokes added the modification notice on 2026-11-20, so the result
differs from that commit.

Without it the greeter quits as soon as LoginSucceeded closes its views, and
its compositor tears down while the user session helper switches VTs. The
greeter session's VT cleanup (VT_SETMODE to VT_AUTO) can drop the pending
switch, so VT_WAITACTIVE blocks until waitForStarted() gives up after 30 s
(sddm/sddm#2043, #2129, PR #2204). With it, the greeter and its compositor
stay up until Display::slotSessionStarted() stops them 5 s after the session
has started.
---
diff --git a/src/greeter/GreeterApp.cpp b/src/greeter/GreeterApp.cpp
--- a/src/greeter/GreeterApp.cpp
+++ b/src/greeter/GreeterApp.cpp
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+// Modified by 9Spokes on 2026-11-20: backported upstream commit da0b64d so the
+// greeter outlives the user session's VT switch.
 /***************************************************************************
 * Copyright (c) 2015-2018 Pier Luigi Fiorini <pierluigi.fiorini@gmail.com>
 * Copyright (c) 2013 Abdurrahman AVCI <abdurrahmanavci@gmail.com>
@@ -361,6 +363,10 @@
         qputenv("QT_IM_MODULE", inputMethod.toLocal8Bit());
 
     QGuiApplication app(argc, argv);
+
+    // Don't quit when the last screen and thus the last view disappears
+    app.setQuitOnLastWindowClosed(false);
+
     SDDM::SignalHandler s;
     QObject::connect(&s, &SDDM::SignalHandler::sigtermReceived, &app, [] {
         QCoreApplication::instance()->exit(-1);
